              "feedback": {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Incorrect. According to the Bronsted-Lowry definition, an acid is a substance that donates a proton (hydrogen cation H"
                      },
                      {
                        "sup": true,
                        "text": "+"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ") to another substance, and a base is a substance that accepts a proton from another substance. After the acid donates H+ in the forward reaction, the resulting species that lost H"
                      },
                      {
                        "sup": true,
                        "text": "+"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " can now accept H"
                      },
                      {
                        "sup": true,
                        "text": "+"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " through the reverse reaction, and this species is therefore a base and called the conjugate base. Likewise, after the base accepts H"
                      },
                      {
                        "sup": true,
                        "text": "+"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " in the forward reaction, the resulting species that accepted H"
                      },
                      {
                        "sup": true,
                        "text": "+"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " can now donate H"
                      },
                      {
                        "sup": true,
                        "text": "+ "
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "through the reverse reaction, and this species is therefore an acid and called the conjugate acid. Essentially, the two species in a conjugate pair (acid and conjugate base pair, or base and conjugate acid pair) differ from each other by one H"
                      },
                      {
                        "sup": true,
                        "text": "+"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " that can be donated or accepted."
                      }
